# Normalize line endings for ALL text files to LF in the repository AND on checkout, on every
# platform. Source and tests are parsed with line-based and multi-line regexes that assume LF; a
# CRLF checkout (Windows with core.autocrlf) would otherwise break them. git auto-detects binary
# files and leaves them untouched, and the explicit rules below are belt-and-suspenders for the
# binary assets this repo ships so they can never be line-ending converted.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never treated as text (so never line-ending converted or diffed as text).
*.png  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico  binary

# Kept for emphasis even though the global rule already covers them: files whose exact bytes a
# drift-guard / version-sync step matches across a newline must stay LF.
src-tauri/Cargo.lock text eol=lf
src-tauri/Cargo.toml text eol=lf
